{
  "title": "Femoral Anteversion",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4059/femoral-anteversion",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 14 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Femoral Anteversion is a common congenital condition caused by intrauterine positioning which lead to increased anteversion of the femoral neck relative to the femur with compensatory internal rotation of the femur.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with the presence of intoeing combined with an increase in internal rotation of the hip of greater than 70° with an accompanying decrease in external rotation of the hip of less than 20°.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation with parental reassurance as most cases resolve by age 10. Rarely, surgical management is indicated in the presence of less than 10° of hip external rotation in children greater than 10 years of age.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "seen in **early childhood (3-6 years)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "twice as frequent in girls than boys",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can be hereditary",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often **bilateral**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "be cautious of asymmetric abnormalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Femoral anteversion is characterized by",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**increased anteversion of the femoral neck** relative to the femur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**compensatory internal rotation of the femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**lower extremity intoeing**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There are three main causes of intoeing including",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**femoral anteversion** (this topic)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**metatarsus adductus** (infants)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**internal tibial torsion** (toddlers)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a packaging disorders caused by intra-uterine positioning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most spontaneously resolve by age 10",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can be seen in association with other packaging disorders",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**DDH**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**metatarsus adductus**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**congenital muscular torticollis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Is based on degree of anteversion of femoral neck in relation to the femoral condyles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4059/images/screen%20shot%202012-07-22%20at%209.03.31%20am.jpg",
              "caption": "Femoral Anteversion"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "at birth, normal femoral anteversion is 30-40°",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically decreases to normal adult range of 15° by skeletal maturity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "minimal changes in femoral anteversion occur after age 8",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "parents complain of an intoeing gait in early childhood",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "child classically sits in the **W position (see above image)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "knee pain when associated with tibial torsion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "awkward running style",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "when extreme in an older child occasional functional limitations in sports and activities of daily living can occur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "difficulty with tripping during walking or running activities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "can be more symptomatic in those with neuromuscular diseases and brace-dependent walkers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "secondary to lever-arm dysfunction and decreased compensatory mechanisms",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "evaluation for intoeing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**femoral anteversion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hip motion (tested in the prone position)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**increased internal rotation** of >70° (normal is 20-60°)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4059/images/screen%20shot%202012-07-22%20at%208.58.42%20am.jpg",
                              "caption": "Prone hip ROM testing"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "decreased external rotation of < 20° (normal 30-60°)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4059/images/screen%20shot%202012-07-22%20at%208.58.34%20am.jpg",
                              "caption": "Prone hip ER testing"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "anteversion estimated on degree of hip IR when greater trochanter is most prominent laterally",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**trochanteric prominence angle test**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patella internally rotated on gait evaluation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**tibial torsion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "look at thigh-foot angle in prone position",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "normal value in infants- mean 5° internal (range, −30° to +20°)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "normal value at age 8 years- mean 10° external (range, −5° to +30°)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**metatarsus adductus**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "adducted forefoot deformity, lateral border should be straight",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "a medial soft-tissue crease indicates a more rigid deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "evaluate for hindfoot and subtalar motion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "none required typically",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT or MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may be useful in measuring actual anteversion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation and parental reassurance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most cases usually resolve **spontaneously** by age 10",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**bracing, inserts, PT, sitting restrictions do not change natural history**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "derotational femoral osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**< 10° of external rotation** on exam in an **older child (>10 yrs)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "rarely needed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "typically performed at the intertrochanteric level",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "amount correction needed can be calculated by (IR-ER)/2",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Multiple studies have been unable to reveal any association with degenerative changes in the hip and knee when increased anteversion persists into adulthood",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
